@prefix : <http://mee.foundation/ontologies/wikidata-vehicle-makes-subset#> .
@prefix vehicles: <http://mee.foundation/ontologies/vehicles#> .
@prefix wd: <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/> .
@prefix dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@base <http://mee.foundation/ontologies/wikidata-vehicle-makes-subset> .

<http://mee.foundation/ontologies/wikidata-vehicle-makes-subset> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
    owl:versionIRI <http://mee.foundation/ontologies/wikidata-vehicle-makes-subset/1.0.0> ;
    dc:date "2026-08-29"^^xsd:date ;
    owl:versionInfo "Version 1.0.0 - initial hand-curated set of 35 major consumer vehicle manufacturers (car, motorcycle, and bus) verified against live Wikidata."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Wikidata Vehicle Makes Subset"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A hand-curated subset of Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org) — 35 major consumer vehicle
                    manufacturers across car, motorcycle, and bus makers, the piece other/vehicles.ttl's
                    vehicles:hasMake needs, analogous to project_files/ncbitaxon-subset.ttl's role for
                    pets:hasSpecies. This is NOT a full extraction of every manufacturer Wikidata knows about
                    (unlike project_files/vbo-subset.ttl's real full extraction of VBO's pet-relevant breed
                    tree) — Wikidata has no bounded "vehicle manufacturer" scope the way VBO's pet breeds did,
                    so, like project_files/dron-upper.ttl/ncbitaxon-subset.ttl, this stays a hand-picked list
                    rather than an exhaustive one. Each individual reuses its real Wikidata Q-ID directly as
                    its own IRI (e.g. wd:Q53268 for Toyota) rather than a locally-minted equivalent — the same
                    "cite the real upstream identifier" principle NCBITaxon/VBO/DrOn/ChEBI IRIs are cited by
                    throughout this project — verified live against https://query.wikidata.org/sparql and
                    https://www.wikidata.org/w/api.php (2026-08-29). Deliberately typed as
                    owl:NamedIndividual, vehicles:Make rather than owl:Class: unlike NCBITaxon (species) or
                    VBO (breeds), which model their own terms as OWL classes — enabling
                    pets:hasSpecies/pets:hasBreed's class-value-punning — Wikidata models a manufacturer as
                    an instance of a class (e.g. "automobile manufacturer", wd:Q786820), not as a class in
                    its own right, so vehicles:hasMake links to a real individual instead, a deliberate,
                    documented adaptation of the pattern rather than a slip. Wikidata's own content
                    is released under CC0 (public domain dedication), so no attribution obligation applies —
                    even lighter than project_files/vbo-subset.ttl's CC-BY 4.0 terms."""@en .

